laurel 2986: the APSS watchdog (0xf017000) and a report of a stuck CPU. Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/watchdog.md.

[V 2026-11-03 13:46:59, logs/usblog-20261103-071332.txt] A kernel hang: no panic, no pong, only the Power button: it stops the agents' test loop. No driver existed (build-honest.md).
A kernel thread signals each CPU once a second and pets only if each answered in 8 s: bark 12 s (SPI 3: lines, then a panic), bite 20 s (a reset with no CPU); a stuck CPU: bark 20 s, bite 28 s after it stopped. A panic: no pets, one bite in 30 s if it stops before its hold; the hold and our own resets stop the hardware. Each interrupt stamps its CPU with the time and pc: a stuck CPU shows where it last took one.
Self-check: the times and enable must hold, the counter must move; else LAUREL WDOG: off, and the heartbeat alone names a stuck CPU. Kill switch laurelwdog=0. Host test: scripts/laurel/wdog-test.sh. iOS 26: the sleh.c hunk is also in post/9015 (the base owns that file). The stackshot report: post/9016.

